    fix: the occupied-port branch no longer certifies an unauthenticated bind. Addresses CF-192.
    
    Bug. scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh took its occupied-port branch
    (line 302: `ss -tln | grep -q ":$PORT "`) whenever anything already listened on the gateway
    port, and there printed `PASS  port — listening on :$PORT` plus `PASS  status_probe — /api/status
    -> 200` without ever calling check_public_bind_auth. The auth refusal lived only in the
    NOT-listening branch (the CF-071 gateway_start refusal), so a public bind with no
    dashboard.basic_auth sailed through and the run ended `HERMES: PASS`, exit 0. A 127.0.0.1 probe
    proves reachability, not protection — it answers on an unauthenticated 0.0.0.0 gateway too.
    
    Measured at the unfixed tree (listener stub on :10800, config = "model: {}", no dashboard block):
      PASS  port — listening on :10800
      PASS  status_probe — /api/status -> 200
      HERMES: PASS          [exit 0]
    
    Fix. The occupied-port branch now evaluates the same gate the --apply start path already uses —
    check_public_bind_auth, the one shell parser (strict YAML subset + refusal reasons) — instead of
    certifying on listener evidence alone. No second parser was written and
    scripts/node_gateway_auth.py was not touched: it is the WRITER of the block, not the validator,
    and its messages are pinned by other arms. With no non-empty dashboard.basic_auth the branch
    emits ONE named, counted row and nothing else about the probe:
    
      FAIL  port — listening on :10800 (not started by this adapter; auth unverified — a public bind
      needs dashboard.basic_auth in ~/.hermes/config.yaml — block absent)
      HERMES: FAIL (1)      [exit 1]
    
    An occupied port that DOES carry a valid block keeps today's PASS rows, so a gateway a previous
    --apply started is still certifiable. The not-listening branch, the CF-071 refusal wording, the
    status_probe row and the --apply start path are unchanged.
    
    Tests. tests/selftest.sh section 55 (the CF-150 gateway-basic-auth block) gains ARM E: no new
    numbered section, no census change (arms_tree stays 55). It reuses the existing mktemp -d fixture
    and adds (a) $cf150/listen-bin/ss, which exits 0 and prints a real LISTEN line
    `LISTEN 0 128 0.0.0.0:10800 0.0.0.0:*`, selected through cf150_env's new CF150_BIN_PREFIX so the
    shared ss keeps every other arm on the not-listening path; (b) $cf150/listening-home, whose
    config has no dashboard block but which does carry a dummy provider key, so inference_key cannot
    be the row that fails — the port gate is the only thing under test. Two assertions, one run:
    
      E-red    LISTEN + no basic_auth      -> exit nonzero, exactly one named FAIL port row,
                                              HERMES: FAIL (1), no HERMES: PASS, no PASS port /
                                              PASS status_probe, no `unbound variable`/`FAILED:`
                                              decoy, serve never launched.
      E-green  the SAME listener on the home arm B staged basic_auth into -> PASS port /
               PASS status_probe must survive (failing on any listener is not a fix).
    
    Red (arm E against the unfixed adapter):
      FAIL  an occupied :10800 with no dashboard.basic_auth was certified (exit 0)
            ... PASS  port — listening on :10800
            ... PASS  status_probe — /api/status -> 200
            ... HERMES: PASS
    Green (same arm, fixed tree):
      PASS  occupied :10800 without dashboard.basic_auth -> exit 1, named FAIL port row,
            HERMES: FAIL (1), nothing certified
      PASS  occupied :10800 WITH dashboard.basic_auth keeps PASS port / PASS status_probe
            (only inference_key fails)
    Both transcripts, the exact commands and the failed-then-fixed run order:
    docs/audits/code-factory-CF-192.probe.txt. AC2's two green paths are the same run's arm A (free
    port + no auth -> the exact CF-071 refusal, serve never launched) and arm C (free port + valid
    auth -> `PASS  gateway_start — /api/status -> 200`), both still green.
    
    Docs. docs/handbook/chapters/M5-harness.md records the occupied-port behaviour: §1 line count for
    install-hermes.sh, a §7 verification row, the row added to the §9 log-line table, the §10 "Auth
    gate skipped" failure mode rewritten as fixed (with the distinguishing PASS path), and §13 finding
    F5-7.
    
